5,1,1,talk,Minato,,Hello everyone. I want to know if the projects make people too tired. I will look at the coordination group staffing and the time lost to copying records.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,I am concerned about our technical dependencies. I will investigate network coverage at customer plants and in-house developer availability to ensure we can actually deliver.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,"We must be careful about where the money comes from and the long-term costs. I will look into the capital budget and software allowance, and vendor licence pricing.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,May,,I'm more interested in whether these things actually last! I'll check the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts and the record of cross-unit standardization efforts.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with everyone. I'm worried we overlook the small, daily struggles. I'll look into misrouted deliveries in the incident logs and the handling of vendor queries.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Minato,,"@George, do you think the budget includes the cost of people's time? I worry we forget that people have limits.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,That is a fair point. Technical feasibility is often ignored until it is too late. We should balance the budget with actual resource availability.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,"Budgeting is rarely simple. My concern is that we commit funds without knowing which pocket they come from, leading to surprises during renewals.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,May,,"Oh, you're all so serious! But really, why fund a ""perfect"" budget if the project dies in six months? We need to see what actually survived.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Midori,,I think May is right. We should look for solutions that fix the little things that frustrate our staff every single day.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Minato,,I just hope we don't pick something that makes the staff work even harder without any help.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. If we promise a delivery date based on a network we don't control, we are just setting ourselves up for failure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,I will keep a close eye on the licensing. A low initial cost often hides a very expensive renewal fee next year.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,May,,Exactly! It's all about the long game. I want to see if we're just repeating the same mistakes over and over.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Midori,,I'm looking forward to seeing if the incident logs show a pattern. Maybe the best project is the one that stops the most daily errors.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm a bit nervous, but I'll do my best to help.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,Let us proceed then. I believe these choices cover the main risks.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,George,,Agreed. Let us see what the data tells us.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,May,,This should be interesting! I'll be waiting to see if any of you found something surprising.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Midori,,I hope we can find a balance that makes everyone's work life a little easier.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
