35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that some people are doing way too much work by hand. They are copying things over and over, and the coordination group is very small.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,My findings are worrying. We have significant gaps in network coverage at customer sites and our internal developers are completely unavailable for months.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The capital budget is frozen, but we have some software allowance. However, per-head licensing will be a nightmare for our budget next year.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"I knew it! The big, fancy rollouts that required everyone to participate just died. Only the small, specific tools for one group actually survived.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,I found that we are wasting time on the same mistakes. We have duplicate addresses and we keep asking vendors for the same certificates.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, if the developers are busy, will the new project just make the coordination group do more work?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"Precisely. If we choose a high-maintenance tool, we will be relying on people who are already overstretched or on networks that don't work.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"This confirms my fear. If we go for a per-head license, the cost will balloon as we scale, and we have no capital budget to cover it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"So, we need something simple. No ""company-wide"" mandates. We need a targeted solution that doesn't require a whole army to maintain.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I agree with May. We have these small, repetitive losses—like the misrouted deliveries—that could be fixed without a massive system overhaul.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,I really don't want to add more to the people who are already tired. Can we pick something that removes the copying work?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"We must avoid anything that requires heavy on-site network access or immediate developer support. A simple, standalone tool would be safer.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,I will only support a proposal that uses a fixed-fee structure or fits within the existing software allowance without creating a renewal crisis.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"Let's be honest: if it's a ""grand vision"" project, it's going to fail. Let's look for the ""boring"" project that actually works.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I think we are all agreeing that a simple, targeted fix for operational waste is the way to go. It's better than an impressive-sounding failure.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I feel a bit better now that we are thinking about the people.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am glad we are considering the infrastructure. It is better to be realistic than optimistic.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I will remain cautious. I want to see the specific costs before I commit my vote.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,I'm just glad we're finally looking at the patterns. Let's see the candidates and pick the one that won't be forgotten in a year.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'm hopeful. Let's find a solution that brings harmony to the daily workflow.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
