60,3,1,talk,Minato,,I like Option A. It helps with the status summaries and notes. It sounds like it would stop people from having to write the same things over and over.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I must object to Option D. My research showed that network coverage at customer plants is terrible. A sync-heavy app would be a disaster.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"Option C is interesting, but I worry about the licensing. If it's a per-user license for every unit, it will be too expensive. Is it a fixed-fee build?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C is exactly the kind of ""standardization"" that usually fails. It's too broad. Option A is small and targeted, which is why it would actually survive.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,I strongly support Option C. I found that we have duplicate addresses and are asking for the same certificates repeatedly. A Supplier Data Hub fixes exactly that.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, would Option C make the coordination group do more work to keep the records clean? I don't want them to be more tired.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,Option A is the safest. It doesn't require on-site network access and doesn't seem to need heavy developer support once the basic tool is set up.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"If Option C is a simple repository, it might fit the software allowance. But Option A seems even lower risk in terms of long-term costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. Option B is too fancy, and Option D is a technical nightmare. Option C is a bureaucratic dream that usually becomes a ghost town. Option A is the winner.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Minato, I think it would actually reduce their work. Right now, they are dealing with the mess of misrouted deliveries. Fixing the data source stops the errors.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I see... if it stops the mistakes, then it helps. But Option A feels like it helps the people who are tired right now.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I cannot support Option D or B. B requires too much production effort, and D is impossible with our current network reality. I'll go with A.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"I've thought about it. Option C is useful, but the risk of a renewal price hike for a company-wide hub is too high. Option A is a smaller, more manageable cost.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"See? We're all seeing the pattern. Small, useful, and low-maintenance. Option A is the only one that doesn't look like a future failure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I still feel Option C addresses the most actual waste on the floor. Misrouted deliveries are a real problem, not just a convenience issue.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm still torn, but I think I'll go with Option A because it helps the people writing the notes.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I'll stick with A. It's the only one that respects our technical constraints.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,I will vote for A. It is the most fiscally responsible choice and avoids the licensing traps I fear.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I'm voting for A. It's the only one that fits the pattern of what actually survives in this company.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,I will vote for C. I believe we should prioritize fixing the errors that affect our customers and our staff's daily stress.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
